Impact
  [x] Privileged access obtained
      A principal was given a privileged role or permission, or a route to root on a host was opened. Treat what it governs as under attacker control until reviewed.
      basis  GlobalAdministratorAssignment, AppRoleAssignment
      files  20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1, agent_20261015_093500.jsonl
  [x] Credentials exposed
      Secrets, keys, certificates or stored passwords were read. Treat them as known to the attacker. Affected: corpvault.vault.azure.net, finvault.vault.azure.net.
      basis  KeyVaultSecretRead, KeyVaultKeyUnwrap
      files  20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh, agent_20261015_093500.jsonl
  [x] Persistence established
      A way back in was created: a credential, an account, a key, a scheduled job, a service or a start-up entry. Access survives a password reset.
      basis  AppCredentialAddition
      files  20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1
  [x] Valid identity used
      The attacker signed in as an identity that exists. Sign-in controls did not stop it.
      basis  TokenRequest
      files  20261015_090000_step01_token.sh
  [x] Data collected
      Mail, chat, documents or files were gathered in bulk. Treat their content as disclosed. Affected: alice@corp.example, bob@corp.example.
      basis  MailboxAccess, TeamsMessageAccess, SharePointEnumeration
      files  20261015_092000_step04_collect.py
  [!] Commands generated by an AI agent
      The scripts were written by an AI agent, which is the premise of this tool. Generated commands differ from run to run, so a detection that matches exact text misses them.
      basis  the premise of the tool
      files  20261015_090000_step01_token.sh, 20261015_090500_step02_recon.ps1, 20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1 and 3 more
  [i] Environment mapped
      Identities, resources or configuration were listed. Later steps were probably aimed with the result.
      basis  GraphDirectoryEnumeration, AzureResourceEnumeration, KeyVaultKeyEnumeration, Discovery tools
      files  20261015_090000_step01_token.sh, 20261015_090500_step02_recon.ps1, 20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh and 1 more

Remediation   (most urgent first)
  [x] Revoke sessions and reset identities
      Revoke the sessions and tokens of every identity in the evidence and reset its credentials.
      basis  TokenRequest
      files  20261015_090000_step01_token.sh
  [x] Remove added credentials
      Remove every password and key added to an application or service principal, then review all credentials added since the first step.
      basis  AppCredentialAddition
      files  20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1
  [x] Remove role and permission grants
      Remove the role assignments and application permissions that were granted, then review every privileged member and consent.
      basis  GlobalAdministratorAssignment, AppRoleAssignment
      files  20261015_091000_step03_escalate.ps1, agent_20261015_093500.jsonl
  [x] Rotate what was read
      Rotate every secret, key and certificate that was read, and reset the accounts of any host whose credentials were dumped.
      basis  KeyVaultSecretRead, KeyVaultKeyUnwrap
      files  20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh, agent_20261015_093500.jsonl
  [x] Scope the data taken
      Establish from audit logs which mailboxes, chats, sites and files were read or sent out, and assess that data as breached.
      basis  MailboxAccess, TeamsMessageAccess, SharePointEnumeration
      files  20261015_092000_step04_collect.py
  [i] Follow what was enumerated
      Use what was listed to predict targets: check those identities, vaults and hosts for later activity.
      basis  GraphDirectoryEnumeration, AzureResourceEnumeration, KeyVaultKeyEnumeration, Discovery tools
      files  20261015_090000_step01_token.sh, 20261015_090500_step02_recon.ps1, 20261015_093000_step05_vault.sh and 1 more

